{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>I will divide them in Jacob.</b> That they would not be established as a bloc. <b>And scatter them in Israel,</b> that they would not gather together. And so it was: the inheritance of Simeon fell within the inheritance of the children of Judah, as it says (Joshua 19:9): ״ויהי נחלת בני שמעון בתוך נחלת בני יהודה״. And their cities were dispersed, one from another, within the territory of Judah, and the inheritance of Levi — the cities of refuge — was scattered throughout all Israel. And the reason he scattered them throughout all Israel was for the benefit of Israel through their rulings, in the manner of what is written of them (Deuteronomy 33:10): ״יורו משפטיך ליעקב ותורתך לישראל״." "<b>And behold,</b> Jacob did not bless Reuben, nor Simeon, nor Levi, but rather reproached them. He reproached Reuben concerning the matter of Bilhah, and Simeon and Levi concerning the matter of Shechem; and from here onward he mentions the rest of the tribes and blesses them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Source citation reads יהושע י ט (Joshua 10:9); the quoted verse is Joshua 19:9. The printed citation is corrupt; normalized."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:26.352413469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}